{
  "$comment": "Component and activation-matrix data read read-only from production on 2026-09-23 via `wp plugin list --status=active-network --fields=name,file,version --format=json` and `wp --url=<site> plugin list --status=active --fields=name,file,version --format=json` for all 11 sites (see network-topology.json). `scope: \"network\"` means network-activated in production; an array of domains means activated on exactly those sites in production. Every plugin defaults to its owning repository's latest GitHub Release asset (`https://github.com/<repo>/releases/latest/download/<asset>`) or, for WordPress.org-hosted third-party plugins, `https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/<wporgSlug>.zip`. `homeboy rig up` never activates a plugin through wp-codebox's own extra_plugins activation (which can only pick network-wide vs the single current blog) -- run.mjs mounts every plugin with activate:false and applies this exact per-site/network activation matrix itself via fixtures/network-activate.php so multi-site products land on the right sites.",
  "theme": {
    "slug": "extrachill",
    "repo": "Extra-Chill/extrachill-theme",
    "asset": "extrachill.zip",
    "settingsKey": "extrachill_theme_source",
    "note": "wp_codebox_extra_themes / inputs.extra_themes only accepts a remote https zip as of Automattic/wp-codebox#2519 (merged into wp-codebox main 2026-09-21 as v0.27.0). The wp-codebox CLI installed on this host is still v0.26.12 (packages/cli/dist not yet rebuilt past 'release: v0.26.12'), which only accepts an absolute local directory path. run.mjs auto-detects which mode to use from the value supplied in extrachill_theme_source: an https://...zip URL is passed straight through to inputs.extra_themes (forward-compatible, will start working the moment the installed CLI updates); anything else is treated as a local checkout path and mounted the way wordpress-multisite-e2e's run.mjs already does. There is no default: callers must supply extrachill_theme_source (a local checkout of the theme (themes/extrachill in Extra-Chill/extrachill), or eventually its release zip)."
  },
  "excludedComponents": [
    {
      "slug": "wp-codebox",
      "scope": "network",
      "reason": "This rig runs the whole network inside a WP Codebox sandbox; mounting the WP Codebox WordPress companion plugin a second time inside its own disposable sandbox is out of scope and would be self-referential."
    },
    {
      "slug": "chubes-gallery-lightbox",
      "scope": "network",
      "reason": "chubes4/chubes-gallery-lightbox has no GitHub Releases and is not listed on WordPress.org, so there is no zip to source by default. A local override can be added the same way extrachill_theme_source works once this is needed."
    },
    {
      "slug": "wp-coding-agents-integration",
      "scope": [
        "extrachill.com"
      ],
      "reason": "Agent-runtime development tooling (wp-coding-agents bridge), not network product code the deploy gate is meant to verify."
    },
    {
      "slug": "intelligence",
      "scope": [
        "studio.extrachill.com"
      ],
      "reason": "Private repository with no public source, per NETWORK-ARCHITECTURE.MD ('the installed repository is not publicly linkable'). Requires a local override to include in a run."
    },
    {
      "slug": "mediavine-control-panel",
      "scope": [
        "extrachill.com",
        "events.extrachill.com",
        "wire.extrachill.com"
      ],
      "reason": "Proprietary vendor plugin Mediavine distributes directly to publisher accounts; there is no public zip to source."
    },
    {
      "slug": "redis-cache",
      "scope": "network",
      "reason": "Requires a Redis server the disposable runtime does not run. Its activation hook (which the rig now fires for real) installs the object-cache.php drop-in; with no Redis reachable, every persistent option/site-option read fails through to defaults and the boot breaks (all network plugins read as inactive). Production runs Redis; the sandbox documents the exclusion instead of pretending."
    }
  ],
